{"architectures":["x64"],"id":"SomePythonThings.ElevenClock","latestVersion":"4.4.1.1","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"description":"Freedom for your Windows 11 Clock.","license":"GPLv3","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/marticliment/ElevenClock/blob/main/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-GB":{"locale":"en-GB","longDescription":"The whole point of ElevenClock is to have a customisable clock on your Windows 11 taskbars.\nWhen Microsoft’s engineers were creating Windows 11, they forgot to add a clock on the secondary screen taskbar.\nSo I did that.\nElevenClock was an app designed to return this functionality back, but it has evolved and it can now replace your system clock in order to let you customise it, adding seconds, moving it around, changing its colour and much more, like in the good old days.","moniker":"elevenclock","tags":["eleven-clock","11clock","clock-with-seconds","clockwithseconds","customise","time-format","windows-taskbar","win11taskbar","windows11taskbar","xp89hz8svwtt0m"]},"en-US":{"description":"Freedom for your Windows 11 Clock.","license":"GPLv3","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/marticliment/ElevenClock/blob/main/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"The whole point of ElevenClock is to have a customizable clock on your Windows 11 taskbars.\nWhen Microsoft’s engineers were creating Windows 11, they forgot to add a clock on the secondary screen taskbar.\nSo I did that.\nElevenClock was an app designed to return this functionality back, but it has evolved and it can now replace your system clock in order to let you customize it, adding seconds, moving it around, changing its color and much more, like in the good old days.","moniker":"elevenclock","name":"ElevenClock","packageUrl":"https://github.com/marticliment/ElevenClock","publisher":"Martí Climent","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/marticliment/ElevenClock","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/marticliment/ElevenClock/releases/tag/4.4.1.1","tags":["eleven-clock","11clock","clock-with-seconds","clockwithseconds","customize","time-format","windows-taskbar","win11taskbar","windows11taskbar","xp89hz8svwtt0m"]}},"longDescription":"The whole point of ElevenClock is to have a customizable clock on your Windows 11 taskbars.\nWhen Microsoft’s engineers were creating Windows 11, they forgot to add a clock on the secondary screen taskbar.\nSo I did that.\nElevenClock was an app designed to return this functionality back, but it has evolved and it can now replace your system clock in order to let you customize it, adding seconds, moving it around, changing its color and much more, like in the good old days.","moniker":"elevenclock","name":"ElevenClock","packageUrl":"https://github.com/marticliment/ElevenClock","publisher":"Martí Climent","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/marticliment/ElevenClock","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/marticliment/ElevenClock/releases/tag/4.4.1.1","tags":["eleven-clock","11clock","clock-with-seconds","clockwithseconds","customize","time-format","windows-taskbar","win11taskbar","windows11taskbar","xp89hz8svwtt0m"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/4.4.1.1/app.json","detailSha256":"f03a4f1d161a0bb14c050cf2e7ea3abf3e10c962a99dd8c43a5d0d1ca32bd41e","releaseDate":"2024-08-03","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"4.4.1.1"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/4.4.0/app.json","detailSha256":"2be706014cd103c08f88f14d1bb39a483f25d4d72061aa43770dc1231994658c","releaseDate":"2024-07-26","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"4.4.0"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/4.3.3/app.json","detailSha256":"78eaee7b7b6736d7a70cfa6d30e1924f0f107804cc24bcbe77f0d1db7a3d5b2f","releaseDate":"2023-11-25","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"4.3.3"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/4.3.2/app.json","detailSha256":"6981f9f1820aae96331e4f561b6dbfc3d9390311442fc5aa768b2ac83910fbcb","releaseDate":"2023-10-24","re